title: Education
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: lwusp_in_government and education_minister_party = 'LWUSP' and education_science_timer = 0
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/walda.jpg
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet


# - change the educational curriculum (only once per 3 years) - will have a "major" and "minor" option:
# - democratic education - focus on critical thinking and democratic values rather than authoritarian teaching. (+ democratization, pro_republic)
# - scientific education - focus on the sciences, mathematics, and technical skills (+ NMC, science)
# - humanistic education - focus on literature, history, and philosophy. (+ NMC, pro_republic if democratization is high)
# - traditional education (reduces relations with DDP)

# - increase educational opportunities for working-class families.
# - Secularize education (+ DVP, instant Zentrum vonc)


= Education 

Education in Sordland is in a sorry state. In a grey area between the central government and the local municipalities, it more often than not teaches backwards concepts such as creationism and still shows remains of Soll's propaganda machine. Now that we are in control of the Ministry of Education, we are able to change all of this.

[? if major_curriculum: Current educational curriculum - [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +] ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @privatize: Privatize education.
- @desollinization: Enact the De-Sollinization Decree.
- @rural_education_institutes: Rural Education Institutes.
- @gender_equality: Gender equality in education.
- @scholarship: Fund scholarships for poorer families.
- @children_for_future: Draft the Children for Future Act.
- @structure: Change the structure and funding of education.
- @creationism: Deal with creationism in schools.
- @curriculum: Change the educational curriculum.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@privatize
subtitle: This would bring us more funds. +1 budget.
view-if: privatized_education <= 2
on-arrival: cps_relation -= 5; pfjp_relation += 3; cwusp_relation -= 2; rwusp_relation -= 4; workers_lwusp -= 3; unemployed_lwusp -= 3; old_middle_lwusp += 1*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress -= 0.5; budget += 1; privatized_education += 1; liberal_strength += 3; liberal_dissent -= 3

While disliked by <span style="color: #7e0b80;">Sollists</span> and <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> as well as the poorer segments of our voter base, privatizing education makes it possible to invest more money in it in the future.

@desollinization
subtitle: This will **irreversibly** tank our relation with the Conservatives.
view-if: desollinization = 0
on-arrival: cps_relation += 5; pfjp_relation += 5; wpb_relation += 5; cwusp_relation -= 5; rwusp_relation -= 15; nfp_relation -= 5; nationalism -= 6; pro_republic += 2; socialism += 1; rural_cwusp -= 5; rural_rwusp += 5; old_middle_cwusp -= 3; new_middle_cwusp -= 3; old_middle_rwusp += 3; new_middle_rwusp += 3; coalition_dissent += 2 if in_usp_coalition; desollinization += 1

We have enacted the De-Sollinization Decree, removing <span style="color: #7e0b80;">Sollist</span> propaganda from schools and democratizing education. The Conservatives hate this move and will from now on always try to obstruct us in every possible way.

@rural_education_institutes
subtitle: Develop education in rural areas. [? if privatized_education = 0 : -1 budget. ?][? if privatized_education > 0 : -2 budget. ?]
view-if: rural_education < 3
on-arrival: budget -= 1; budget -= 1 if privatized_education > 0; unemployed -= 0.5; economic_growth += 2; rural_lwusp += 3*(1-dissent); bluds_lwusp += 1*(1-dissent); rural_nfp -= 1; rural_education += 1

We have focused our efforts in expanding the school system in rural areas.

@gender_equality
subtitle: Pass a decree enforcing gender equality in the schools.
view-if: gender_equality_education = 0
on-arrival: womens_rights += 1; gender_equality_education += 1; pfjp_relation += 5; cps_relation += 3; rwusp_relation -= 3; nfp_relation -= 5; workers_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_lwusp += 3*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 1

Schools are now gender equal! This is a historical step on the way towards full emancipation.

@scholarship
subtitle: This is popular among the workers and unemployed. -1 budget.
on-arrival: public_hs += 1; workers_lwusp += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.2; economic_growth += 0.5; budget -= 1

We have funded more scholarship programs for children from poorer families.

@children_for_future

// TO DO

@structure

Education in Germany has traditionally been organized on religious and class lines. Schools are often either Protestant or Catholic (or rarely <span style="color: #005EB8;">Jewish</span>), and religious classes are required in most mixed-denomination schools. In addition, the working class has at most eight years of public education in primary and middle schools, while the middle and upper classes have access to private schools and Gymnasiums that prepare students for universities. Thus, the universities tend to be dominated by <span style="color: #3E88B3;">conservatives</span> and <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span>, which has negative consequences for bureaucratic recruitment.

- @secularize
- @public_hs
- @school_boards
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organization.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize
title: Support secular schools to end the religious dominance in education.
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -1 budget - requires a majority of parties to support secular schools.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and ((progressive_coalition + dvp_r >= 50 and not lvp_formed) or (kpd_r + spd_r + lvp_r >= 50 and lvp_formed))
view-if: secularized = 0
go-to: secularize_menu if not in_social_liberal_coalition and not in_spd_majority and not in_left_front; secularize_2 if in_social_liberal_coalition or in_spd_majority or in_left_front

@secularize_menu

Are you sure about this? The <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> Coalition had an agreement to not touch religious schools; the Catholic [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] will revolt.

- @secularize_2: Yes, do it.
- @ed_menu: No, do not touch religious education.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize_2
on-arrival: secularized = 1; secularized_a = 1; budget -= 1; catholics_spd -= 15; catholics -= 5; z_relation -= 15; dvp_relation += 6*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 6*(1-dissent); lvp_relation += 6*(1-dissent); kpd_relation += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5; new_middle_ddp += 4; new_middle_dvp += 4; new_middle_lvp += 8; dvp_left += 3; ddp_left += 3; ddp_cohesion += 2; lvp_left += 5; education_goal_spd += 1
go-to: vote_of_no_confidence.vonc_menu if (in_weimar_coalition and not in_social_liberal_coalition) or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or in_emergency_government

# instant VONC from zentrum

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>, [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, [? if not dvp_exist: former ?]<span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?], and <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> vote in favor of secular education, overcoming the opposition of the religiously-oriented [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. We have funded secular community schools to replace some previous denominational schools.

[? if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or in_emergency_government: Of course, the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] is in revolt at this proposal, and have called for a vote of no confidence in our government. ?]



@public_hs
title: Increase educational opportunities for the working class by funding public high schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; public_hs += 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); prussian_police_loyalty += 0.04; education_science += 0.5; unemployed -= 0.1; economic_growth += 0.2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent); dvp_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; education_goal_spd += 1
max-visits: 3

# this makes the bureaucracy more proletarian
We have funded more public secondary schools so that proletarian children may receive the same education as middle and upper-class children, and can be prepared for universities.


@school_boards
title: Create elected school boards to give local areas more control over education.
on-arrival: school_boards += 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2; education_goal_spd += 1
view-if: school_boards = 0

We have created local elected school boards, and delegated some of the decision-making for local schools to them.

@creationism

